---
import BaseLayout from "../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import Timeline from "../components/charts/Timeline.astro";
import { career, markets, stack } from "../data/profile";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Hani Yacoub, fraud and AI-abuse analyst in Berlin. Six years across cloud, fashion, automotive, and energy."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap ab__inner">
      <div class="ab__lead" data-reveal>
        <span class="label">About</span>
        <h1 class="ab__statement">
          I'm Hani. I find fraud in large account populations and prove it
          before anyone acts on it.
        </h1>
      </div>

      <div class="ab__body" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120">
        <p>
          German-Jordanian, based in Berlin, working in Arabic, German, and
          English. I started in energy markets, moved through automotive and
          fashion, and now work on fraud prevention at AWS. Different
          industries, but underneath it was always the same job: a large
          population, a small group abusing it, and decisions that are
          expensive to get wrong in either direction.
        </p>
        <p>
          The part I take most seriously is false positives. A missed
          fraudster costs money. A wrongly banned customer costs money and
          trust, and usually surfaces weeks later as a support ticket nobody
          connects back to the rule that caused it. So I build carve-outs
          before bulk actions, treat every flag as a claim that still needs
          evidence, and measure whether a control worked with a holdout
          instead of a before-and-after chart that flatters it.
        </p>
        <p>
          At AWS I build the tooling as well as the analysis: the data
          platform my investigations run on, LLM agents that gather evidence
          and get checked by other agents, a population-wide graph that makes
          fraud rings visible, and enforcement jobs with safety gates I can
          defend line by line. Before that, at Zalando, I owned fraud metrics
          for business reviews and built the Remaining Fraud Damage measure
          across six European markets. None of it is exotic. It holds up
          because it gets verified.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap ab__arc">
      <Timeline label="The arc" items={[...career]} />
    </div>

    <div class="wrap ab__grid">
      <div class="ab__col" data-reveal>
        <span class="label">Markets covered</span>
        <p class="ab__markets mono">{markets.join(" · ")}</p>
        <p class="ab__note">
          Zalando Risk &amp; Abuse fraud analytics, top six European markets.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ab__col" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="90">
        <span class="label">Stack</span>
        <ul class="ab__stack" role="list">
          {stack.map((s) => <li class="mono ab__tool">{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .ab__inner { display: grid; gap: var(--space-7); }
  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .ab__inner {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
      gap: var(--space-9);
    }
  }
  .ab__lead { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-4); }
  .ab__statement {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    font-weight: 520;
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    max-width: 17ch;
  }
  .ab__body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-5); }
  .ab__body p {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }
  .ab__body em { font-style: italic; color: var(--ink); }

  .ab__arc {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 5vw, 5rem);
    padding-top: var(--space-7);
    border-top: var(--hair) solid var(--line);
  }

  .ab__grid {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-7);
  }
  @media (min-width: 46rem) {
    .ab__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr; gap: var(--space-9); }
  }
  .ab__col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); }
  .ab__markets {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .ab__note { font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--muted); max-width: 30ch; }
  .ab__stack { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-3); }
  .ab__tool {
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    color: var(--muted);
    border: var(--hair) solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 100px;
    padding: 0.3em 0.9em;
    transition: border-color var(--dur-1) var(--ease-out), color var(--dur-1) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .ab__tool:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--ink); }
</style>
